meta {
  name: SuperAdmin
  seq: 22
}

docs {
  The Super Admin API (`/api/super-admin/v1`): back-office operations for the
  people running the platform. It is a separate surface with its own accounts
  and tokens; a user token never works here and a Super Admin token never
  works on the user API.

  ## Switching it on

  Everything is behind one master flag. With `SUPER_ADMIN_ENABLED=false` (the
  default) none of these routes exist.

  ## Getting in

  1. Create the first owner on the server:
     `php artisan super-admin:create you@example.com --role=owner`
     (it prints a one-time temporary password).
  2. `Auth/Login`: you get a setup token. `Auth/Change Password`, then
     `Auth/2FA - Enable` and `Auth/2FA - Confirm` (save the recovery codes).
  3. `Auth/Login` again, then `Auth/2FA - Verify`. `superAdminToken` is now set
     and every request in this folder uses it.

  ## Conventions

  Sensitive writes take `reason` and a fresh `totp_code`; the lighter ones take
  only `reason`. Every change lands in `Audit Log/List`. List requests store
  the first row's id (`saAccountId`, `saUserId`, `saWorkspaceId`, ...) so the
  rest of each folder works.
}
